# state: first-run   (NFS MW has no golden profile, so every run is first-run)
# Need for Speed: Most Wanted (4541007B), lane.perdrawon1010: the race start the owner measured on 10-09.
# Quick Race -> Custom Race -> Sprint, default track (Diamond & Union), Opponents 2 (3 racers), Fiat Grande
# Punto, Auto: every menu step read from frames (passes 1-3, 1-1791641530-perdrawon1010-3932477,
# 1-1791642016-perdrawon1010-4029199, 1-1791643217-perdrawon1010-95991). Twelve race starts per boot: the
# first after the menus, eleven more by STANDINGS (d-pad up) -> Y Restart -> OK (the prompt opens on Cancel).
# Timing, from pass 3's frames: GO comes ~21 s after the transmission A (21.0 and 21.6 s in passes 3 and 2)
# and ~4.1 s after a restart's OK (4.2, 4.2, 4.0 s; a restart does not reload, the countdown runs at once).
# Each start holds RT (gas) from before GO, writes `mark gameplay` (first) or `mark go<N>` ~1.5 s BEFORE GO
# so the mark's screencap is done before the race starts, drives ~11 s past GO, shoots a frame, lets go.
# startread.py (docs/lanes/perdrawon1010/) reads the 10 s after GO as mark + 1.5 .. mark + 12.
#
# lane.nfsroute1011 (10-11, #433): 2 of the last 8 runs on this route measured the wrong screen
# (1-1791741306-nfsdefault1011-87778: lost the two main-menu right taps, fell back into the name
# keyboard; 1-1791741301-nfsdefault1011-87617: drifted off-step from s07 on, ending on attract
# footage). Both void runs diverge first at s07's keyboard, the densest run of zero-hold d-pad taps
# in this file. Fix, from docs/lanes/nfsroute1011/NOTES.md: every `axis HATX/HATY max/min` tap
# immediately followed by `mid` now holds 0.12 s first (NFS reads the hat axis, not BTN_DPAD_*,
# confirmed from pad.sh and this route's own good runs); and a `waitfor` now gates every press that
# depends on a screen (first-run prompts, each menu step, and the restart loop's OK), scored
# against refs/nfs-mw-quickrace/*.png (score table and thresholds in NOTES.md). No existing `wait`
# duration changed, so this route still pools with its earlier runs for lane.nfsdefault1011's A/B
# arms; a waitfor only extends the existing wait with a poll, and aborts (ROUTE FAIL) instead of
# measuring a screen that never arrived.
wait 13.3
shot s01-publisher_logo
# step 1 [publisher_logo] This is an early boot logo animation (green polygon emblem on white), before any title or menu. No p
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 11.0
shot s02-intro_video
# step 2 [intro_video] The previous step was a publisher logo, and this is a cinematic-style showcase with no menu or promp
press START 120
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 10.4
shot s03-intro_video
# step 3 [intro_video] Static EA title art with a copyright line and no menu or prompt yet, so it is not gameplay. The prev
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 6.8
shot s04-save_load_prompt
waitfor alias-prompt 20 160,195,970,460 5
# step 4 [save_load_prompt] Save/alias prompt; per the hints, prompts that create a save: Yes is fine and reaches play. The high
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 7.9
shot s05-save_load_prompt
waitfor autosave-notice1 20 160,195,970,460 5
# step 5 [save_load_prompt] Autosave notice with only an OK button highlighted; no Yes/No choice, so A confirms it and moves the
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 7.3
shot s06-save_load_prompt
waitfor autosave-notice2 20 160,195,970,460 5
# step 6 [save_load_prompt] Autosave notice with only an OK button; no Yes/No choice. A confirms it and returns to the game.
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 11.0
shot s07-name_entry
waitfor name-entry-cursor 30 230,345,230,60 5
# step 7 [name_entry] Previous DOWN A and A presses only typed letters and returned here. The cursor is on the letter A, n
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 0.6
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 0.6
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 11.6
shot s08-save_load_prompt
waitfor alias-save-prompt 30 160,195,970,460 10
# step 8 [save_load_prompt] Save prompt with No highlighted. Earlier DOWN A (choosing Yes) looped back to the name keyboard, so 
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 7.0
shot s09-save_load_prompt
waitfor autosave-disabled 20 160,195,970,460 5
# step 9 [save_load_prompt] Only an OK button is shown, the same autosave notice seen before. Earlier A presses on this notice r
press B 120
wait 0.6
wait 9.0
shot s10-save_load_prompt
waitfor autosave-disabled 20 160,195,970,460 5
# step 10 [save_load_prompt] Only one button (OK) exists, so there is no Yes/No choice. B did nothing on this unchanged screen, a
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 6.2
shot s11-save_load_prompt
waitfor autosave-disabled 20 160,195,970,460 5
# step 11 [save_load_prompt] Only one button (OK) exists, so this is a notice with no Yes/No choice. START and B already did noth
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 20.6
shot s12-main_menu
waitfor main-menu 20 500,650,680,300 0.6
# main menu (Career, Challenge Series, Quick Race, ...): Quick Race is two right of Career
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 1.2
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 1.5
shot mm-quickrace
waitfor mm-quickrace 10 500,650,680,300 3
press A 120
wait 4
# quick race (Quick Play, Custom Race, Split Screen): Custom Race is one right
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 1.5
shot qr-custom
waitfor qr-custom 10 500,650,680,300 3
press A 120
wait 4
# custom race mode select (Circuit, Sprint, Drag, Lap Knockout, Speedtrap): Sprint is one right
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 1.5
shot cr-sprint
waitfor cr-sprint 10 500,650,680,300 3
press A 120
wait 4
# sprint track select opens on the default track, Diamond & Union (1/44)
shot cr-track
waitfor cr-track 10 0,60,1180,140 5
press A 120
wait 4
# sprint options (Traffic Level, Opponents, Difficulty, Catch Up; Opponents defaults to 3):
# Opponents is one down; one left takes it 3 -> 2, so 3 racers
axis HATY max
wait 0.12
axis HATY mid
wait 1.2
axis HATX min
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 1.5
shot cr-opp2
waitfor cr-opp2 10 130,300,1020,200 5
press A 120
wait 4
# car select opens on Stock 1/32, Lexus IS 300; the Fiat Grande Punto is one right (2/32)
axis HATX max
wait 0.12
axis HATX mid
wait 1.5
shot cr-punto
waitfor cr-punto 10 0,60,1180,160 5
press A 120
wait 3
# transmission prompt opens on Auto
shot cr-auto
waitfor cr-auto 10 150,290,980,380 5
press A 120
# start 1: frames every ~2.5 s through the load and countdown, RT from ~3.5 s before GO
wait 2
shot s1-02
wait 2
shot s1-04
wait 2
shot s1-06
wait 2
shot s1-08
wait 2
shot s1-10
wait 2
shot s1-12
wait 2
shot s1-14
wait 0.5
axis RT max
wait 1.9
mark gameplay
wait 12.4
shot s1-g11
axis RT min
